WEBVTT

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.600
Immelmann?

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:08.020
Arad, why are you with the son of that man?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.900
Never mind.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.700
Sorry. Thanks for saving me. I owe you.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.410
What was that about?

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.210
I guess he didn't get along with your old man.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.840
Don't worry about it.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.500
You knew my father too?

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.720
In passing. He was a pilot just like us.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.980
He was a pilot? My father?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.100
Yeah.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.430
Why have you been quiet about that?

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.670
Because you never asked.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.860
Are you really gonna give me that crap?

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.930
<i>Our kiss will send us leaping to the edge of space</i>

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.360
<i>Our affection is too hot for mere passionate love</i>

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.210
<i>We can be in absolute zero</i>

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.010
<i>I'll spark a dream in you</i>

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:23.530
<i>I'll embrace all you believe in</i>

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.150
<i>Let your genes go wild</i>

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>I love you so much, but I try to play it cool sometimes</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.880
<i>Tear off my mask and squeeze me to a whole new dimension</i>

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:43.850
<i>By banging into each other, we confirm our uncovered love</i>

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.250
<i>The tears we can't cry on our own connect us to the future</i>

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:54.870
<i>Our passionate love will shoot us into a super nova-like state</i>

00:01:54.870 --> 00:02:00.760
<i>We can do this! No wounds can hold us back if we're together</i>

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.480
<i>Show me your passion, pray to the skies</i>

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.850
<i>Our super big bang will breathe life into a new genesis</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.110
<i>We burn our lives for this fusion</i>

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:15.590
<i>We are in absolute zero</i>

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.320
Thanks for your patronage!

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.720
Do come by again!

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.570
Thanks for helping with the restaurant.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:31.000
We need all the help with Mari not around!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.200
No biggie!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.920
Freyja's the best poster girl ever!

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:41.230
Poster girl? I like the sound of that.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.860
Her laugh is always so creepy.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.100
She's keeping herself busy so she can forget about her worries.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.900
Putting on a cheerful mask.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:55.070
Her home planet just declared war on the entire galaxy.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.280
Here's your jellyfish ramen!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.890
Looks delicious!

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.060
Actually, I've got an idea!

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.160
What is it?

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.460
Makina's smile is always so lovely.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.090
That pose is lovely too!

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.660
I know, right?

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.630
Wait, wrong page.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.350
Freyja's profile?

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.600
What about it?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.880
Did you...

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.080
Yup! You catch on quick!

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.720
November 3, the day after 
tomorrow, is Fre-Fre's birthday!

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.140
I was thinking about throwing a surprise party for her.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.270
A surprise party?

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:32.980
I'm in!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.980
I'll take care of the details with Rei-Rei.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.940
I can cover the food!

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.270
Everyone should get a birthday present for her.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.570
It's gonna be great!

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.410
Yes!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.370
Yes!

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.080
Uh...

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.000
Yes.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.450
That's right!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.670
A present, huh?

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.380
Windermere has the capability 
to conquer the entire galaxy.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:08.600
I thought it was weird that such a tiny nation would pick a fight with NUNS.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.400
However, they haven't made a move yet.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.140
Increasing the output of the song must have strained the Wind Singer,

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.700
leading them to hold back for now.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.610
Is that right, Mikumo?

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.170
Yes.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:27.620
I came into contact with the Wind Singer through the ruins before.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.960
If we could use the structures that appeared at the ruins, we might be able to fight back.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.340
However, that's just a hypothesis.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:43.930
I suggest we investigate the 
structures while the enemy is silent.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:49.140
Their eyes are set on the galactic 
stage, so now's our chance?

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:50.500
Yes.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:53.810
Mikumo!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.470
Thanks for that.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.480
Don't read too much into it.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.090
Yeah.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.320
Are you going to Freyja's surprise party?

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.660
Perhaps. I'll give it some thought.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.080
Oh?

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.000
She'll give it some thought, huh?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.030
Why do I have to be here?

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.360
I have no idea what to get her.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.220
And you need to get her something too, right?

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.180
Somehow, I knew this is how it would play out.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.560
Wow, you've looked up stuff already? Way to go, Mir—

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.320
Wait, these are pricey.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.000
You're the most boorish of men.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.640
We're talking about a birthday present for a lady!

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:47.070
Isn't this just a list of stuff you want?

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.570
No!

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:53.080
It's the results of the "what I want for my 
birthday" poll from this month's Daisy Daisy!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.510
Right...

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:58.920
Gosh. What's your budget? I hope you've at least considered that.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.430
Really?

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:06.470
Presents aren't about the price tag, but the feelings you put into them!

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:07.630
Let's go.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.190
Oho, things are looking smooth.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:20.610
I can feel that awkwardness of couples who've only just started going out.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.060
This isn't right either.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.150
"Did you find something nice?"

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.240
"Well..."

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:33.850
"What do you think about this?"

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.160
"It's so cute!"

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.690
"No, it's not."

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.750
"Nothing can be called cute compared to you."

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.660
"Oh, Hayate, you're so sweet!"

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.250
What a great way to spend a day off.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.260
This is tougher than I thought it'd be.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.010
What would make her happy?

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:56.170
You know her way better than I do.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.270
You think so?

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.310
What does she like?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.270
Other than singing and apples, I really have no clue.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.780
Do you fancy her?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:09.700
Wow!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.950
Right to the point!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.250
Where did that come from?

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.660
She's just... Well, not just a friend...

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.750
Not a partner either...

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.870
A comrade, perhaps?

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.780
Anyway, she's never boring.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:27.440
Pretty fun, actually.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.300
Things tend to end up pretty crazy when she's around.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.560
I see.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:37.220
Aren't those the signs of a blossoming love?

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.140
Do you think so?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.940
A-According to the literature!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.150
Oh, I thought you were speaking from experience.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.780
O-Of course I'm not.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.910
Romance and dating aren't exactly my forte.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:57.100
Sure, I've been invited to grab drinks a few times,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.680
but I don't think that counts...

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.120
How about this?

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.460
I have trouble believing my eyes.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.420
He's denser than a black hole.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.920
Love is cruel.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:21.100
The preparations are complete for the experiment to further increase the song's power.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:26.530
We should act before the NUNS can gather their forces.

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:27.390
Considering the burden on you—

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.360
That is none of your concern.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.530
Let us act.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.530
Are you certain?

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:38.270
My mission is to unite all people of the galaxy through the song of the wind.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:43.270
I believe your suggestion is the best way to end this war.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:44.960
Is it not, Roid?

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.670
Your Majesty.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.880
To achieve this goal, no burden is too great.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.370
Very well. Your is wish is our command, Your Majesty.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.310
Isn't this a good opportunity?

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.680
That's right!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.600
We can take the entire galaxy at once!

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:09.430
We tainted our wings black to defend the honor of Windermere!

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:13.780
That was when we fought the NUNS.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:18.990
Obviously, all we need to do is follow His Oh-So-Wise Majesty's will!

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:23.980
I wonder what the White Knight thinks of this.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.620
The same as you.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:30.040
He loved apples when he was little.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:36.920
After every flight training, he'd drink fresh apple juice, saying it was the best thing ever.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:39.970
That's how it was

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:49.880
The war's not ending.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:10:02.870
<i>The stars are aligning, an occasion once in 30 years</i>

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:10.210
<i>I don't want to sleep, just sitting next to you</i>

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:14.870
<i>lost in admiration</i>

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.460
How about this, Second Lt. Hayate?

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:15.180
What's wrong?

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:24.350
<i>I can feel the wheels turning little by little</i>

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.930
Hayate?

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.500
Oh, sorry. I must be hungry.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.350
Just felt dizzy for a second.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.810
You scared me.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.770
<i>A year? A day? A moment?</i>

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.480
Mikumo?

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.510
Windermere lies beyond that constellation.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.060
Are you reminiscing about home?

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:43.020
Looking at the stars just brought up some memories.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.390
The wind of Windermere is bitingly cold.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.320
It stings your face.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.920
Have you been there before?

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:59.800
Have you ever sung on that stage on Windermere?

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.960
I haven't.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:03.860
I see.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:14.550
The song rides the wind all the way to the stars before fading away.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:20.700
Here, dessert's on me.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:30.410
Should you really be treating me 
when you're already low on cash?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:33.320
It's the least I could do after 
dragging you along with me all day.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.550
I see. Thanks.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:48.680
Umm... It's quite a coincidence that your father was a pilot too.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:49.970
I guess.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.390
What's wrong?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:58.600
Just that I've been to all these planets and tried doing different jobs,

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:02.330
but nothing ever felt right.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.120
Then when I finally found my passion,

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.120
it turns out to be the same as my dad's.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.990
It feels really weird to end up on the same path as him.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:16.920
But you chose to be a pilot before you found out about him, right?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.510
I suppose.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.570
They're not related at all!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.300
You picked your own path.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.760
It's just who I am, huh?

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.620
That's right.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:36.100
I know it's not so simple though.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.900
Yeah.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.310
Mirage, thanks for everything today!

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.130
What about the present?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.090
The Windermereans broadcasted this footage?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.880
Perhaps the day the truth is revealed is coming close.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.390
Yeah. Just don't mention it to Hayate.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.700
I know.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.140
But don't think you can keep it a secret from him forever.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.360
I suppose.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.650
She's sleeping.

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:23.860
So defenseless.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.410
Take this!

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:31.900
Okay!

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.660
This should do it, right?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.790
Help me a little!

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.000
Decorations?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.210
All good!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.060
Here too!

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:38.920
Done!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.130
Food?

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:41.590
Okay!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.820
Captain Arad, stop slacking off!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.920
How's the cake?

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.040
Just gimme a sec!

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.600
By the way, where did Hayate run off to?

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:56.310
Don't tell me he's still looking for a present...

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.770
Target located.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.620
ETA: three hundred seconds.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:03.690
Copy that!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.610
Freyja's coming!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.080
Already?!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.560
What is Hayate doing?!

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.360
Captain, you're in the way!

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:17.780
It's pitch dark.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:24.130
I'm back...

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.220
Where did everyone go?

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.680
Wh-Wh-What the hecks?!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.640
One, two...

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.810
Happy birthday!

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.200
Birthday?

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.690
Wait, today's my birthday?!

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.400
You forgot?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:52.790
For my past few birthdays, the mayor would always tell me to get married already,

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:54.660
so I had to run away.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.100
For real?

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.370
Sounds tough!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:01.790
Where's Hayate?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.760
Jeez.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:12.010
Presents from all of us!

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:13.900
So many!

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:14.720
Is this really okay?

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:20.560
Mikumo?

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:21.930
Kumo-Kumo?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.270
That's rare.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.860
Thanks for coming, Mikumo.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>Happy birthday! Happy birthday!</i>

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:37.910
<i>Happy birthday to you!</i>

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:46.420
<i>Wishing the best dear Freyja!</i>

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:51.250
<i>Happy birthday! Happy birthday!</i>

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:56.390
<i>Happy birthday to you!</i>

00:15:56.390 --> 00:16:05.220
<i>Happy birthday to you!</i>

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.400
Freyja!

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.110
Make a wish!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.170
Thanks! Thanks!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.960
Thank you all so much!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.340
Some words from the birthday girl!

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:33.590
Okay!

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.270
Crap, I've gotta hurry!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:47.390
Well... When I was little, war was going on,

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:51.780
but our village was in the countryside, so we really didn't see much of it.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.240
But it was still pretty tough.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:17:00.470
That was when I encountered music from Earth.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:04.640
When my father went with the wind...

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:07.750
When my mother went with the wind...

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.030
The grief, the solitude...

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:19.130
The sadness were all blown away by the happy songs.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:25.180
I didn't really get it but I felt that singing was amazing.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:32.230
So when I heard there were auditions, I was determined to join Walküre.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.700
Then I actually made it through the auditions

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.280
and I was really so happy.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.650
Where were you?

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.870
Don't worry about it.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:58.510
Today, I turned 15.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:03.260
It's the halfway point of a Windermerean's life.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.690
It's a really important day for me...

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.710
This is wonderful...

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:09.440
Fre-Fre...

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.510
I'm so happy to have met all of you!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:20.700
I'll keep singing so that I'll have no regrets!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.420
Fre-Fre!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.040
I'm so happy I got to meet you!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:31.750
There, there.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.520
Shall the party begin then?

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.680
Look at this!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.720
Come over here!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.140
What's that?

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:49.690
Snow?

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.150
Snow!

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.570
Snow!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.320
It's snowing!

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.540
Nice.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.810
So this is why he was late?

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.250
I've never seen snow before!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.590
Deculture!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.560
Happy birthday, Freyja.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.120
Hayate?

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:33.520
Sorry for running late.

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:39.030
Wait... Did you make it snow?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.480
Kinda.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.470
It's my birthday present to you.

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:49.770
Thankies, Hayate!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:50.660
You like it?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.130
I love it so much!

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.840
Your rune's shining.

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:08.970
<i>I close my eyes and think of a wish</i>

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:15.480
<i>I don't say it, but I'm sure it'll come true</i>

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:21.420
<i>I can feel your chest rise and fall</i>

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:28.030
<i>I'll never forget this moment, locked in your gaze</i>

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:34.440
<i>My heart's overflowing with emotions (with emotions)</i>

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:39.880
<i>So often tears come falling out of nowhere (out of nowhere)</i>

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:50.970
<i>Don't let go of the pieces of fate that connect us</i>

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.410
<i>God bless you</i>

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:58.320
<i>We met in the light of the wind</i>

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:05.820
<i>I won't hesitate anymore, my heart is burning so hot</i>

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:10.620
<i>Maybe you've known this all the way</i>

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:19.880
<i>Thanks for the days you stayed by my side watching over me</i>

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:23.510
<i>Thank you</i>

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:30.000
You actually came.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.970
I wanted to see what it was like.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:37.440
Nobody ever celebrated my birthdays.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.650
Mikumo?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.620
Snow? Not half bad.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.640
Would you tell me about my father?

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:56.880
He was a skilled pilot.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.500
I owe him plenty.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.590
And...

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:06.500
He was too kind for his own good.

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:16.350
Mission 16: Hesitating Birthday

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:13.930
<i>God bless you</i>

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:18.770
<i>I had no idea you could love someone this much</i>

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:26.400
<i>I don't think this passion could ever be undone</i>

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:31.210
<i>It's my only joy in this world</i>

00:22:31.210 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>We share our happiness and we wipe each other's tears</i>

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:56.660
<i>If in your heart there's a drop of (blue sadness)</i>

00:22:57.330 --> 00:23:07.690
<i>Let's unleash an arrow of light (and take it down)</i>

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:23.410
<i>This is a miracle, so God, please keep guiding our love</i>

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:11.780
Freyja...

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:28.020
Huh? Why am I...

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.730
Next time: Scatter on Stage
